WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.000
The origins of Luca's sea monsters may be
a mystery;

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.950
however, Pixar's new movie has several curious
connections with Monsters Inc, and could even

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.040
explain how the Supers from The Incredibles
got their powers.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.590
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining all the hidden links

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.610
between Luca, Monsters Inc, and the Incredibles
movies.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:24.680
To understand where Luca's sea monsters may
come from we need to revisit a few key moments

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.860
from Pixar's OG creature feature, Monsters
Inc.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.430
In that film, monsters travel through doors
which act as portals to the human world where

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.430
they harvest screams for energy to power their
own monster world.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:40.750
And although the monsters make it their business
to be as scary as possible to children, they

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.650
themselves are absolutely terrified of human
beings.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.520
"The kid almost touched me.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.770
She got this close to me.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.270
I could have died."

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:54.120
In the monster world, humans are considered
so incredibly toxic that even a stray item

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.720
of clothing on a monster's back has to be
destroyed via a controlled explosion.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:04.530
The affected monster is also forcibly decontaminated
by shaving off all their hair and disinfecting

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.530
them.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:10.100
So, when a live human child, Boo, comes through
a door and is discovered on the loose in the

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.970
monster city, a full-blown panic ensues.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.150
Given all that, could you imagine how the
inhabitants of Monstropolis might react to

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.920
seeing one of their fellow monsters suddenly
transform into a human, like the sea monsters

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.050
are able to do in Luca?

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:28.470
There is, in fact, an amusing version of this
in Luca itself, when we see Daniella's reaction

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:33.040
to what she calls a "land monster" when she
mistakes her husband Lorenzo for a human.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.040
"It's me!"

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.040
"Oh!

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.050
You scared the scales off of me!"

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.430
"Wow, we look horrifying."

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:44.010
In the world of Monsters Inc, we know that
the concept of banishment, a form of punishment

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:48.880
that involves sending away monsters to live
in the human world permanently, already exists.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:49.880
"Loch Ness.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:50.880
Bigfoot.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.880
The Abominable Snowman.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.500
They all got one thing in common pal.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.500
Banishment!"

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.220
It was used against Mike and Sulley when they
uncovered Mr Waternoose and Randall's plot;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.990
and in Monsters University, it's implied that
tampering with the mail at the factory mailroom

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.230
was the reason the Abominable Snowman was
banished to the Himalayas.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:12.159
And although we see monsters learning underwater
skills at the School of Aquatics in Monsters

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:15.519
University,
if one of them suddenly took on a human form

00:02:15.519 --> 00:02:19.489
after emerging from the water, we can assume
that the other monsters would be extremely

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:23.860
fearful and suspicious of them, perhaps going
so far as to banish them.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:28.709
And what if the Loch Ness Monster, who's been
mentioned as existing in the Pixar universe,

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:30.409
was one of these monsters?

00:02:30.409 --> 00:02:35.120
Obviously, we're talking about fiction here,
but perhaps the reason the existence of Nessie

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.219
has never been proven is because it has the
ability to come out of the water and disguise

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:40.790
itself as a human.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:45.909
Could the Loch Ness Monster be a monster-human
hybrid species like Luca and Alberto?

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:49.980
Legends of the Loch Ness Monster date back
as far as the sixth century, and although

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.290
Loch Ness is in Scotland, there would be plenty
of time for that monster to use its human

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:58.590
form to mix with the human population, in
time for its descendants to end up in the

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.829
Italian Riviera near Portorosso.

00:03:00.829 --> 00:03:05.620
A Monsters Inc character who has somewhat
related powers to Luca's sea monsters is the

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.999
villain Randall Boggs, who has the power of
camouflage to a much greater degree than real-life

00:03:10.999 --> 00:03:12.209
chameleons.

00:03:12.209 --> 00:03:16.640
Randall isn't a shapeshifter, but he can change
his skin to blend into his surroundings, and

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.930
although he initially can't control his ability
in Monsters University, by the time of Monsters

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.480
Inc he's in full charge of his powers.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.860
Perhaps the sea monsters in Luca then have
a related gene to Randall, except they don't

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.900
seem to be able to fully control switching
it on and off like him.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:38.140
Which could even imply the skin-changing power
evolves between the time of Luca and Monsters

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.140
Inc.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:43.450
An alternate Monsters Inc connection with
Luca could be via an origin story that was

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.709
first released with the Monsters Inc DVD called
"History of the Monster World".

00:03:47.709 --> 00:03:51.749
Hat tip to the Carlin Brothers who noticed
this in their Luca monster theory video.

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:56.809
The Monsters Inc bonus short film tells the
story of "two primitive tribes, the Mans and

00:03:56.809 --> 00:03:57.809
the Mons".

00:03:57.809 --> 00:04:01.319
Although the Mons wanted to be friends with
the Mans, the Mans disliked them for their

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:04.949
appearance and smell and so they drove the
Mons away.

00:04:04.949 --> 00:04:09.860
Notice how Luca's villain Ercole also comments
about Luca and Alberto's odour and bullies

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.109
them like the Mans did to the Mons.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:13.109
"Oof.

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:15.120
And he smells like behind the pescheria."

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.450
The Mons swam away and ended up on an enchanted
island where they ate magical fruits and vegetables

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:25.010
that made them bigger and gave them characteristics
of other animals that ate those foods on the

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.090
island.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:30.590
And when the Mons discovered the scary appearance
they'd taken on, they came up with the idea

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:35.550
to get back at the Mans by sneaking up on
them and scaring them, ultimately making it

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.660
their mission in life.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.770
Now, what's interesting about this is that
in an early version of Luca, the sea monsters

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:45.430
had their own town on a separate island where
they lived, as you can see in this concept

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.430
art.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.920
The monster town idea was scrapped in the
end, however, the island was kept as the location

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:55.670
of Alberto's tower, and there's still a reference
to the original idea of monsters living there

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.670
in this clip.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.780
"Do we really need to fish near the island?"

00:04:58.780 --> 00:04:59.780
"You worry too much."

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:00.780
"I don't know.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.830
What if the old stories are true?"

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.980
So, how do we get from Luca's sea monsters
with their powers of transformation to the

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:08.540
Supers of The Incredibles?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:13.480
Well, for starters the period setting of Luca
aligns fairly well with that of the Incredibles

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:14.480
movies.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.320
There are various easter eggs in Luca to films
from the 1950s like 20,000 Leagues Under The

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.880
Sea, Roman Holiday, and La Strada.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.100
The movie's end credits show Luca and Giulia
watching the moon landing which took place

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:32.490
in 1969, and Luca's director Enrico Casarosa
has said the film is set around the 50s and

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:33.490
60s.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:37.800
As for The Incredibles, going by the newspaper
that Mr Incredible reads in the first movie,

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.070
it's implied that film takes place in 1962.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.260
Although in an interview with Bustle, The
Incredibles director Brad Bird said his intention

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:49.270
wasn't to specify too precisely the year that
the movie takes place.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:54.640
Instead, it's just supposed to be in an era
which feels like the 60s, and Bird even suggested

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:58.310
he would have removed the date on the newspaper
if he'd taken it in.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:03.070
With monster-human hybrids like Luca going
out into the world, it shows how the genes

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:07.340
which give him his transformation powers could
spread into the human world.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:12.250
Or alternatively, Luca's keen interest in
astronomy could also lead him to come into

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:17.420
contact with NASA where his special abilities
would undoubtedly generate interest in him

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:21.940
from other government agencies, who in turn
might unlock the key or gene that gives him

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:22.940
his powers.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:27.730
Both of these possibilities, where Supers
either have their powers from birth like Jack-Jack,

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.900
or acquire them say through experiments or
accidents,

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:35.300
could fit with what Brad Bird has said about
the origins of his characters' powers, as

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.490
he considers both as potentially where their
extraordinary abilities come from.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:43.580
In an interview with Cinema Blend, Bird said,
"If we have a baby with superpowers, that

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.820
means they can be born.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:49.440
Although, I wouldn't say that every superhero
in this universe is naturally created.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.620
Maybe there are some toxic spills in there."

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:56.900
Now, it's unlikely that Luca himself is the
sea monster directly responsible for any genetic

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:01.550
origins of the Supers, as we know from the
first Incredibles movie that Supers were already

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:06.960
operational in the 1940s,
but Luca mixing with the human world demonstrates

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.530
how genetic mutations could spread if his
ancestors before him already left the sea

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.460
and mingled with the human population.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:18.210
After all, we know Luca's grandmother has
been regularly going into the human town for

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:19.210
a long time.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.210
"Mom!

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.210
What are you doing here?"

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.810
"I come to town most weekends."

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:26.670
And the two old ladies have also been living
among the humans for years.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:31.370
On top of that, we know that Alberto's father
went missing one day, and perhaps one possibility

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:35.670
is that that he fell in love with a human
and went to live on land, in a spin on Guillermo

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.550
del Toro's The Shape of Water.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:43.260
So, I had a lot of fun thinking up and theorising
about these curious connections between Luca,

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:46.810
Monsters Inc, and The Incredibles,
and if you want to discover all the Pixar

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:51.669
easter eggs I found in the movie to the likes
of Inside Out, Finding Nemo, and Up, tap here

